ow reference is a snapshot position, not a participant ID. Return for any reason is Iowa\u2019s definition.","sha256":"74a1b7b5299e1033849dc617de75e01a3385302560d9e579c6dfd8efc13285fe"},{"id":"aws","title":"AWS Open Data discovery","publisher":"Registry of Open Data on AWS","url":"https://registry.opendata.aws/","geography":"Global","type":"Discovery only \u00b7 not ingested","publication":"Checked October 24, 2026","detail":"Searched the registry for prison and recidivism datasets. No suitable direct outcome dataset was found. Common Crawl was assessed as a possible web-evidence source.","limitations":"Common Crawl is not an outcome registry. Anonymous S3 bucket listing returned AccessDenied. No AWS-hosted outcome data is represented in this application; no AWS infrastructure was provisioned."},{"id":"calctra-stories","title":"California rehabilitation alumni stories","publisher":"CALCTRA \u00b7 State of California","url":"https://www.calctra.ca.gov/success-stories/","geography":"California","type":"Public stories \u00b7 not a cohort dataset","publication":"Discovered October 24, 2026","detail":"Official adult alumni stories describe training and published post-release employment milestones. Useful as source material illustrating what a dated, documented milestone looks like.","limitations":"Stories are selectively published, not a representative release cohort. No alumni identities are imported into this app. Do not calculate recidivism or infer program causation from these stories. Publication does not authorize unrelated personal research."},{"id":"juvenile-recidivism","title":"California juvenile recidivism reports","publisher":"CDCR \u00b7 Office of Research","url":"https://www.cdcr.ca.gov/research/juvenile-recidivism/","geography":"California \u00b7 juvenile system","type":"Historical aggregate reports \u00b7 not ingested","publication":"FY 2013\u201314 and FY 2014\u201315 release cohorts listed","detail":"Separate youth reports measure three-year arrest, conviction, and return to state custody, including juvenile or adult state institutions.","limitations":"Historical youth cohorts are separate from the adult-prison TPW brief. These reports do not provide a named youth roster or current participant follow-up. No juvenile participant identities are collected in this app."},{"id":"juvenile-population","title":"California Juvenile Detention Profile Survey","publisher":"Board of State and Community Corrections","url":"https://www.bscc.ca.gov/jdps-dashboard/","geography":"California \u00b7 county juvenile facilities","type":"Population data \u00b7 discovered, not ingested","publication":"Dashboard through Q2 2026 \u00b7 updated September 25, 2026","detail":"Queryable state/county facility population data and trends. Useful for describing juvenile facility scale and demand; raw data can be accessed through the linked official query tool.","limitations":"Facility populations are not participant outcomes or three-year recidivism. Collection varies by agency, some dashboard values are imputed, and revisions can change historical figures. Not a source of named participant identities."}]}